en:
Happy is the one who has not followed the counsel of the wicked,
or taken the path of sinners,
or joined the company of the insolent;

Ask it of Me,
and I will make the nations your domain;
your estate, the limits of the earth.

O ETERNAL One, lead me along Your righteous [path]
because of my watchful foes;
make Your way straight before me.

For there is no sincerity on their lips;
their heart is [filled with] malice;
their throat is an open grave;
their tongue slippery.

Condemn them, O God;
let them fall by their own devices;
cast them out for their many crimes,
for they defy You.

But let all who take refuge in You rejoice,
ever jubilant as You shelter them;
and let those who love Your name exult in You.

I am weary with groaning;
every night I drench my bed,
I melt my couch in tears.

then let the enemy pursue and overtake me;
let my life be trampled to the ground,
and my body dwell in the dust.    Selah.

Rise, O ETERNAL One, in Your anger;
assert Yourself against the fury of my foes;
bestir Yourself in my behalf;
You have ordained judgment.

GOD judges the peoples;
vindicate me, O ETERNAL One,
for the righteousness and blamelessness that are mine.

Let the evil of the wicked come to an end,
but establish the righteous;
the One who probes the mind and conscience is God the Righteous.

You blast the nations;
You destroy the wicked;
You blot out their name forever.

The enemy is no more—
ruins everlasting;
You have torn down their cities;
their very names are lost.

Have mercy on me, O ETERNAL One;
see my affliction at the hands of my foes,
You who lift me from the gates of death,

GOD is known,
having worked judgment;
the wicked are snared by their own devices. Higgaion. Meaning of Heb. uncertain.    Selah.

Rise, O ETERNAL One!
Let not mortals have power;
let the nations be judged in Your presence.

Their ways prosper at all times;
Your judgments are far beyond them;
they snort at all their foes.

They lurk in outlying places;
from a covert they slay the innocent;
their eyes spy out the hapless.

They wait in a covert like a lion in a lair;
wait to seize the lowly;
they seize the lowly as they pull their net shut;

You will listen to the entreaty of the lowly, O ETERNAL One,
You will make their hearts firm;
You will incline Your ear

GOD is in the divine holy palace;
GOD—whose throne is in heaven,
whose eyes behold, whose gaze searches humankind.

For GOD is righteous,
and loves righteous deeds;
the upright shall behold God’s face.

Help, O ETERNAL One!
For the faithful are no more;
the loyal have vanished from among mortals.

People speak lies to one another;
their speech is smooth;
they talk with duplicity.

Look at me, answer me, O my ETERNAL God!
Restore the luster to my eyes,
lest I sleep the sleep of death;

Anyone who lives without blame,
who does what is right,
and in their heart acknowledges the truth;

whose tongue is not given to evil;
who has never done harm to a compatriot,
or borne reproach for [acts toward] a neighbor;

for whom someone contemptible is abhorrent,
but who honors those who fear GOD;
who keeps an oath even when it hurts;

I say to GOD,
“You are my Sovereign, my benefactor;
there is none above You.”

You will teach me the path of life.
In Your presence is perfect joy;
delights are ever in Your right hand.

You have visited me at night, probed my mind,
You have tested me and found nothing amiss;
I determined that my mouth should not transgress.

I call on You;
You will answer me, God;
turn Your ear to me,
hear what I say.

Rise, O ETERNAL One! Go forth to meet my enemies.
Bring them down;
rescue me from the wicked with Your sword,

Then the earth rocked and quaked;
the foundations of the mountains shook—
rocked by divine indignation;

The way of God is perfect;
the word of the ETERNAL is pure.
[God] shields all who seek refuge.

You have granted me the shield of Your protection;
Your right hand has sustained me,
Your care has made me great.

I struck them down,
and they could rise no more;
they lay at my feet.

You have rescued me from the strife of people;
You have set me at the head of nations;
peoples I knew not must serve me.

His rising-place is at one end of heaven,
and his circuit reaches the other;
nothing escapes his heat.

and from willful sins keep Your servant;
let them not dominate me;
then shall I be blameless
and clear of grave offense.

For the king trusts in GOD;
through the faithfulness of the Most High
he will not be shaken.

For they schemed against You;
they laid plans,
but could not succeed.

My God,
I cry by day—You answer not;
by night, and have no respite.

All who see me mock me;
they curl their lips,
they shake their heads.

“Let him commit himself to GOD;
let [God] rescue him,
let [God] save him,
for [God] is pleased with him.”

Do not be far from me,
for trouble is near,
and there is none to help.

My life ebbs away:
all my bones are disjointed;
my heart is like wax,
melting within me;

my vigor dries up like a shard;
my tongue cleaves to my palate;
You commit me to the dust of death.

Dogs surround me;
a pack of evil ones closes in on me,
like lions [they maul] my hands and feet.

For [God] did not scorn, and did not spurn,
the plea of anyone lowly;
[God] did not turn away from them;
when they cried out, [God] listened.

Let the lowly eat and be satisfied;
let all who seek GOD give praise.
Always be of good cheer!

All those in full vigor shall eat and prostrate themselves;
all those at death’s door, whose spirits flag,
shall bend the knee in submission.

to come;
they shall tell of the beneficence to people yet to be born,
for [God] has acted.

A psalm of David.
GOD is my shepherd;
I lack nothing.

Though I walk through a valley of deepest darkness,
I fear no harm, for You are with me;
Your rod and Your staff—they comfort me.

You spread a table for me in full view of my enemies;
You anoint my head with oil;
my drink is abundant.

ב my God, in You I trust;
may I not be disappointed,
may my enemies not exult over me.

ה ו guide me in Your true way and teach me,
for You are God, my deliverer;
it is You I look to at all times.

ז O ETERNAL One, be mindful of Your compassion
and Your faithfulness;
they are old as time.

ח Be not mindful of my youthful sins and transgressions;
in keeping with Your faithfulness consider what is in my favor,
as befits Your goodness, O ETERNAL One.

ש Protect me and save me;
let me not be disappointed,
for I have sought refuge in You.

Of David.
Vindicate me, O ETERNAL One,
for I have walked without blame;
I have trusted in GOD;
I have not faltered.

Do not hide Your face from me;
do not thrust aside Your servant in anger;
You have ever been my help.
Do not forsake me, do not abandon me,
O God, my deliverer.

Look to GOD;
be strong and of good courage!
O look to GOD!

Of David.
O ETERNAL One, I call to You;
my rock, do not disregard me,
for if You hold aloof from me,
I shall be like those gone down into the Pit.

GOD’s voice is over the waters;
the God of glory thunders,
GOD, over the mighty waters.

GOD’s voice causes hinds to calve,
and strips forests bare;
while in the divine temple all say “Glory!”

I extol You, O ETERNAL One,
for You have lifted me up,
and not let my enemies rejoice over me.

I seek refuge in You, O ETERNAL One;
may I never be disappointed;
as You are righteous, rescue me.

Incline Your ear to me;
be quick to save me;
be a rock, a stronghold for me,
a citadel, for my deliverance.

O ETERNAL One, let me not be disappointed when I call You;
let the wicked be disappointed;
let them be silenced in Sheol;

Then I acknowledged my sin to You;
I did not cover up my guilt;
I resolved, “I will confess my transgressions to GOD,”
and You forgave the guilt of my sin.    Selah.

You are my shelter;
You preserve me from distress;
You surround me with the joyous shouts of deliverance.    Selah.

Let me enlighten you
and show you which way to go;
let me offer counsel; my eye is on you.

Be not like a senseless horse or mule
whose movement must be curbed by bit and bridle;
far be it from you!

ready the spear and javelin
against my pursuers;
tell me, “I am your deliverance.”

Let disaster overtake them unawares;
let the net they hid catch them;
let them fall into it when disaster [strikes].

But when I stumble, they gleefully gather;
wretches gather against me,
I know not why;
they tear at me without end.

You have seen it, O ETERNAL One;
do not hold aloof!
O my Sovereign, be not far from me!

In bed they plot mischief;
they are set on a path of no good,
they do not reject evil.

Your beneficence is like the high mountains;
Your justice like the great deep;
human and animal You deliver, O ETERNAL One.

Of David.
א Do not be vexed by evildoers;
do not be incensed by wrongdoers;

ה Give up anger, abandon fury,
do not be vexed;
it can only do harm.

ו A little longer and there will be no wicked;
you will look at where they were—
they will be gone.

ק Look to GOD and keep to the godly way,
and you will be raised high that you may inherit the land;
when the wicked are cut off, you shall see it.

My mind reels;
my strength fails me;
my eyes too have lost their luster.

Those who seek my life lay traps;
those who wish me harm speak malice;
they utter deceit all the time.

I was dumb, silent;
I was very in Hos. 10.1; Jonah 4.4. still
while my pain was intense.

My mind was in a rage,
my thoughts were all aflame;
I spoke out:

Tell me, O ETERNAL One, what my term is,
what is the measure of my days;
I would know how fleeting my life is.

You have made my life just handbreadths long;
its span is as nothing in Your sight;
no human endures any longer than a breath.    Selah.

Everyone walks about as a mere shadow;
mere futility is their hustle and bustle,
amassing and not knowing who will gather in.

Hear my prayer, O ETERNAL One;
give ear to my cry;
do not disregard my tears;
for like all my forebears
I am an alien, resident with You.

You, O my ETERNAL God, have done many things;
the wonders You have devised for us
cannot be set out before You;
I would rehearse the tale of them,
but they are more than can be told.

You gave me to understand that
You do not desire sacrifice and grain offering;
You do not ask for burnt offering and purgation offering.

I proclaimed [Your] righteousness in a great congregation;
see, I did not withhold my words;
O ETERNAL One, You must know it.

I did not keep Your beneficence to myself;
I declared Your faithful deliverance;
I did not fail to speak of Your steadfast love in a great congregation.

For misfortunes without number envelop me;
my iniquities have caught up with me;
I cannot see;
they are more than the hairs of my head;
I am at my wits’ end.

But let all who seek You be glad and rejoice in You;
let those who are eager for Your deliverance always say,
“Extolled be GOD!”

But I am poor and needy;
may my Sovereign devise [deliverance] for me.
You are my help and my rescuer;
my God, do not delay.

May GOD guard them and preserve them;
and may they be thought happy in the land.
Do not subject them to the will of their enemies.

where deep calls to deep
in the roar of Your cataracts;
all Your breakers and billows have swept over me.

Send forth Your light and Your truth;
they will lead me;
they will bring me to Your holy mountain,
to Your dwelling-place,

My heart is astir with gracious words;
I speak my poem to a king;
my tongue is the pen of an expert scribe.

You are fairer than all mortals;
your speech is endowed with grace;
rightly has God given you an eternal blessing.

in your glory, win success;
ride on in the cause of truth and meekness and right;
and let your right hand lead you to awesome deeds.

Your arrows, sharpened,
[pierce] the breast of the king’s enemies;
peoples fall at your feet.

You love righteousness and hate wickedness;
rightly has God, your God, chosen to anoint you
with oil of gladness over all your peers.

Royal princesses are your favorites;
the consort stands at your right hand,
decked in gold of Ophir.

is led inside to the king;
maidens in her train, her companions,
are presented to you.

“Desist! Realize that I am God!
I dominate the nations;
I dominate the earth.”

The great of the peoples are gathered together,
the retinue of Abraham’s God;
for the guardians of the earth belong to God,
who is greatly exalted.

The praise of You, God, like Your name,
reaches to the ends of the earth;
Your right hand is filled with beneficence.

Walk around Zion,
circle it;
count its towers,

take note of its ramparts;
go through its citadels,
that you may recount it to a future age.

If I failed to act when you did these things,
you would fancy that I was like you;
so I censure you and confront you with charges.

True sacrifice to God is a contrite spirit;
God, You will not despise
a contrite and crushed heart.

Then You will want sacrifices offered in righteousness,
burnt and whole offerings;
then bulls will be offered on Your altar.

I praise You forever, for You have acted;
I declare that Your name is good
in the presence of Your faithful ones.

For strangers have risen against me,
and those who are ruthless seek my life;
they are unmindful of God.    Selah.

I said,
“O that I had the wings of a dove!
I would fly away and find rest;

I would soon find me a refuge
from the sweeping wind,
from the tempest.”

It is not an enemy who reviles me
—I could bear that;
it is not my foe who boasts against me
—for then I could hide;

[God] redeems me unharmed
from the battle against me;
it is as though many are on my side.

Have mercy on me, O God,
for people persecute me;
all day long my adversary oppresses me.

in God, whose word I praise,
in God I trust;
I am not afraid;
what can mortals do to me?

You keep count of my wanderings;
put my tears into Your flask,
into Your record.

in God I trust;
I am not afraid;
what can mere humans do to me?

who will reach down from heaven and deliver me—
sending down steadfast love;
my persecutor reviles.    Selah.

My heart is firm, O God;
my heart is firm;
I will sing, I will chant a hymn.

People will say,
“There is, then, a reward for the righteous;
there is, indeed, divine justice on earth.”

For see, they lie in wait for me;
fierce people plot against me
for no offense of mine,
for no transgression, O ETERNAL One;

They rave with their mouths,
sharp words are on their lips;
[they think,] “Who hears?”

Do not kill them lest my people be unmindful;
with Your power make wanderers of them;
bring them low, O our shield, my Sovereign,

In Your fury put an end to them;
put an end to them that they be no more;
that it may be known to the ends of the earth
that God does rule over Jacob.    Selah.

But I will sing of Your strength,
extol each morning Your faithfulness;
for You have been my haven,
a refuge in time of trouble.

O God, You have rejected us,
You have made a breach in us;
You have been angry;
restore us!

God promised in the sanctuary
that I would exultingly divide up Shechem,
and measure the Valley of Sukkoth;

Gilead and Manasseh would be mine,
Ephraim my chief stronghold,
Judah my scepter;

Moab would be my washbasin;
on Edom I would cast my shoe;
acclaim me, O Philistia!

From the end of the earth I call to You;
when my heart is faint,
You lead me to a rock that is high above me.

You lay plans to topple them from their status;
you delight in falsehood;
you bless with your mouths,
while inwardly you curse.    Selah.

I rely on God, my deliverance and glory,
my rock of strength;
in God is my refuge.

Trust in [God] at all times, O people;
pour out your hearts before the Holy One;
God is our refuge.    Selah.

Do not trust in violence,
or put false hopes in robbery;
if force bears fruit pay it no mind.

One thing God has spoken;
two things have I heard:
that might belongs to God,

for You are my help,
and in the shadow of Your wings
I shout for joy.

But the king shall rejoice in God;
all who swear by [God] shall exult,
when the mouth of liars is stopped.

They arm themselves with an evil word;
when they speak, it is to conceal traps;
they think, “Who will see them?”

all people shall stand in awe;
they shall proclaim the work of God
whose deed they perceived.

In GOD shall the righteous rejoice
and take refuge;
all the upright shall exult.

You take care of the earth and irrigate it;
You enrich it greatly,
with the channel of God full of water;
You provide grain for all;
for so do You prepare it.

The meadows are clothed with flocks,
the valleys mantled with grain;
they raise a shout, they break into song.

Say to God,
“How awesome are Your deeds,
Your enemies cower before Your great strength;

all the earth bows to You,
and sings hymns to You;
all sing hymns to Your name.”    Selah.

and who turned the sea into dry land:
Israel crossed the river on foot;
we therefore rejoice in [God].

You have let people ride over us;
we have endured fire and water,
and You have brought us through to prosperity.

I offer up fatlings to You,
with the odor of burning rams;
I sacrifice bulls and he-goats.    Selah.

Nations will exult and shout for joy,
for You rule the peoples with equity,
You guide the nations of the earth.    Selah.

God will arise;
all opponents shall be scattered,
and foes shall flee.

Disperse them as smoke is dispersed;
as wax melts at fire,
so the wicked shall perish before God.

But the righteous shall rejoice;
they shall exult in the presence of God;
they shall be exceedingly joyful.

God’s chariots are myriads upon myriads,
thousands upon thousands;
my Sovereign is among them as in Sinai in holiness.

O kingdoms of the earth,
sing to God;
chant hymns to my Sovereign,    selah

You are awesome, O God, in Your holy places;
it is the God of Israel who gives might and power to the people.
Blessed is God.

I am sinking into the slimy deep
and find no foothold;
I have come into the watery depths;
the flood sweeps me away.

I am weary with calling;
my throat is dry;
my eyes fail
while I wait for God.

Let those who look to You,
O my Sovereign, GOD of hosts,
not be disappointed on my account;
let those who seek You,
O God of Israel,
not be shamed because of me.

Rescue me from the mire;
let me not sink;
let me be rescued from my enemies,
and from the watery depths.

Let the floodwaters not sweep me away;
let the deep not swallow me;
let the mouth of the Pit not close over me.

Answer me, O ETERNAL One,
according to Your great steadfastness;
in accordance with Your abundant mercy
turn to me;

do not hide Your face from Your servant,
for I am in distress;
answer me quickly.

You know my reproach,
my shame, my disgrace;
You are aware of all my foes.

For God will deliver Zion
and rebuild the cities of Judah;
they shall live there and inherit it;

Let those who seek my life
be frustrated and disgraced;
let those who wish me harm,
fall back in shame.

But let all who seek You be glad and rejoice in You;
let those who are eager for Your deliverance always say,
“Extolled be God!”

But I am poor and needy;
O God, hasten to me!
You are my help and my rescuer;
O ETERNAL One, do not delay.

Be a sheltering rock for me to which I may always repair;
decree my deliverance,
for You are my rock and my fortress.

While yet unborn, I depended on You;
in the womb of my mother, You were my support;
I sing Your praises always.

saying, “God has forsaken him;
chase him and catch him,
for no one will save him!”

Your beneficence, high as the heavens, O God,
You who have done great things;
O God, who is Your peer!

Of Solomon.
O God, endow the king with Your judgments,
the king’s son with Your righteousness;

So let him live, and receive gold of Sheba;
let prayers for him be said always,
blessings on him invoked at all times.

Let abundant grain be in the land, to the tops of the mountains;
let his crops thrive like the forest of Lebanon;
and let the people sprout up in towns like country grass.

May his name be eternal;
while the sun lasts, may his name endure;
let peoples invoke his blessedness upon themselves;
let all nations count him happy.

Blessed is God’s glorious name forever;
such glory fills the whole world.
Amen and Amen.

As for me, nearness to God is good;
I have made the Sovereign GOD my refuge,
that I may recount all Your works.

No signs appear for us;
there is no longer any prophet;
no one among us knows for how long.

We praise You, O God;
we praise You;
Your presence is near;
people tell of Your wondrous deeds.

There is a cup in GOD’s hand
with foaming wine fully mixed;
from this [God] pours;
all the wicked of the earth drink,
draining it to the very dregs.

The stout-hearted were despoiled;
they were in a stupor;
the bravest of soldiers could not lift a hand.

In my time of distress I turn to my Sovereign,
with my hand [uplifted];
[my eyes] flow all night without respite;
I will not be comforted.

I recall at night their jibes at me;
I commune with myself;
my spirit inquires,

The waters saw You, O God,
the waters saw You and were convulsed;
the very deep quaked as well.

Clouds streamed water;
the heavens rumbled;
Your arrows flew about;

Your thunder rumbled like wheels;
lightning lit up the world;
the earth quaked and trembled.

Your way was through the sea,
Your path, through the mighty waters;
Your tracks could not be seen.

GOD heard and then raged;
fire broke out against Jacob,
anger flared up at Israel,

Do not hold our former iniquities against us;
let Your compassion come swiftly toward us,
for we have sunk very low.

Let the groans of the prisoners reach You;
reprieve those condemned to death,
as befits Your great strength.

O God of hosts, turn again,
look down from heaven and see;
take note of that vine,

imposed as a decree upon Joseph
when he went forth from the land of Egypt;
I heard a language that I knew not.

In distress you called and I rescued you;
I answered you from the secret place of thunder
I tested you at the Waters of Meribah.    Selah.

I the ETERNAL am your God
who brought you out of the land of Egypt;
open your mouth wide and I will fill it.

They neither know nor understand,
they go about in darkness;
all the foundations of the earth totter.

O God, do not be silent;
do not hold aloof;
do not be quiet, O God!

O ETERNAL God of hosts,
hear my prayer;
give ear, O God of Jacob.    Selah.

Better one day in Your courts than a thousand [anywhere else];
I would rather stand at the threshold of God’s house
than dwell in the tents of the wicked.

For the ETERNAL God is sun and shield;
GOD bestows grace and glory,
and does not withhold bounty from those who live without blame.

Let me hear what God, the ETERNAL, will speak,
as a promise of well-being to the faithful ones—this people;
may they not turn to folly.

Preserve my life, for I am steadfast;
O You, my God,
deliver Your servant who trusts in You.

Teach me Your way, O ETERNAL One;
I will walk in Your truth;
let my heart be undivided in reverence for Your name.

O God, arrogant people have risen against me;
a ruthless band seeks my life;
they are not mindful of You.

Turn to me and have mercy on me;
grant Your strength to Your servant
and deliver the son of Your maidservant.

You make my companions shun me;
You make me abhorrent to them;
I am shut in and do not go out.

My eyes pine away from affliction;
I call to You, O ETERNAL One, each day;
I stretch out my hands to You.

From my youth I have been afflicted
and near death;
I suffer Your terrors wherever I turn.

O ETERNAL One, God of hosts,
who is mighty like You, O Yah?
Your faithfulness surrounds You;

North and south—
You created them;
Tabor and Hermon sing forth Your name.

Yours is an arm endowed with might;
Your hand is strong;
Your right hand, exalted.

Then You spoke to Your faithful ones in a vision
and said, “I have conferred power upon a warrior;
I have exalted one chosen out of the people.

May the favor of my Sovereign, our God, be upon us;
let the work of our hands prosper,
O prosper the work of our hands!

With pinions you will be covered;
you will find refuge under God’s wings—
whose fidelity is an encircling shield.

When they call on Me, I will answer them;
I will be with them in distress;
I will rescue them and make them honored;

Surely, Your enemies, O ETERNAL One,
surely, Your enemies perish;
all evildoers are scattered.

GOD is sovereign,
and robed in grandeur;
GOD is robed,
and girded with strength.
The world stands firm;
it cannot be shaken.

Your decrees are indeed enduring;
holiness befits Your house,
O ETERNAL One, for all times.

Their evil will be made to recoil upon them,
through their own wickedness they will be annihilated;
the ETERNAL our God will annihilate them.

for this One is our God,
and we are the people being cared for—the tended flock.
O, if you would but heed God’s charge this day:

Forty years I was provoked by that generation;
I thought, “They are a senseless people;
they would not know My ways.”

Declare among the nations, “GOD is sovereign!”
The world stands firm; it cannot be shaken;
the peoples will be judged with equity.

O you who love GOD, hate evil!
For the lives of the loyal are guarded;
they are saved from the hand of the wicked.

Exalt the ETERNAL our God
and bow down to the divine footstool;
[God] is holy!

[God] spoke to them in a pillar of cloud;
they obeyed those decrees,
the law given to them.

Our ETERNAL God, You answered them;
You were a forgiving God for them,
but You exacted retribution for their misdeeds.

Of David. A psalm.
I will sing of faithfulness and justice;
I will chant a hymn to You, O ETERNAL One.

I will study the way of the blameless;
when shall I attain it?
I will live without blame within my house.

I will not set before my eyes anything base;
I hate crooked dealing;
I will have none of it.

Do not hide Your face from me
in my time of trouble;
turn Your ear to me;
when I cry, answer me speedily.

You will surely arise and take pity on Zion,
for it is time to be gracious to her;
the appointed time has come.

They shall perish, but You shall endure;
they shall all wear out like a garment;
You change them like clothing and they pass away.

Bless the ETERNAL One, O angels,
mighty creatures who do God’s bidding,
